1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,947
等回答的时候，我们的 app 显示：正在思考，11 秒
While you wait for an answer, our app says: thinking, eleven seconds.

2
00:00:04,183 --> 00:00:06,513
回答出来以后，它折叠成一张收据
Afterwards it folds into a receipt:

3
00:00:06,513 --> 00:00:09,708
思考了 22 秒，这是整个等待的时间
thought for 22 seconds, which is the whole wait.

4
00:00:10,028 --> 00:00:12,817
点开，等待分成两段
Open it, and the wait splits in two:

5
00:00:12,817 --> 00:00:17,389
真正的思考只有 13.5 秒，然后是写 8.7 秒
only 13.5 seconds of thinking, then 8.7 seconds of writing.

6
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:19,162
在思考什么？
Thinking about what?

7
00:00:19,212 --> 00:00:22,369
三年前，还没有哪个聊天 app 会给你看模型在思考
Three years ago, no chat app showed you a model thinking.

8
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,689
那为什么我们给你看一个计时器，却从不给你看思考的内容？
And why does ours show you a clock, but never the thoughts?

9
00:00:27,133 --> 00:00:29,074
这个想法比这些 app 更早
The idea is older than the apps.

10
00:00:29,394 --> 00:00:33,250
2022 年 1 月，Google 的研究者发现
In January 2022, Google researchers showed that a model

11
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:37,736
先让模型把步骤写出来，它能解出更多题
solves more problems if you ask it to write out its steps first.

12
00:00:38,056 --> 00:00:40,116
他们把它叫作思维链，chain of thought
They called it chain of thought.

13
00:00:40,166 --> 00:00:43,410
几个月后，一句话就做到了：「Let's think step by step」
Months later, one sentence did it: let's think step by step.

14
00:00:43,730 --> 00:00:45,330
这是写在提示词里的一个技巧
It was a trick in the prompt.

15
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:48,705
2024 年 9 月，OpenAI 发布了 o1
In September 2024, OpenAI released o1,

16
00:00:48,705 --> 00:00:54,681
一个用强化学习训练、先推理再回答的模型
a model trained with reinforcement learning to reason before it answers.

17
00:00:55,001 --> 00:00:57,769
OpenAI 选择不展示原始的思考内容
OpenAI chose not to show the raw thoughts,

18
00:00:57,769 --> 00:01:02,909
理由是用户体验、竞争优势，以及可以监控这些思考
citing user experience, competitive advantage, and the chance to monitor them,

19
00:01:02,909 --> 00:01:06,072
它改为展示一段由模型写的摘要
and showed a summary written by a model instead.

20
00:01:06,316 --> 00:01:07,916
别家做了不同的选择
Others chose differently.

21
00:01:08,065 --> 00:01:11,799
DeepSeek 的 R1 把推理文本交给了开发者
DeepSeek's R1 handed its reasoning text to developers.

22
00:01:12,119 --> 00:01:15,959
Claude 3.7 展示了原始的思考内容，作为研究预览
Claude 3.7 showed its raw thinking, as a research preview.

23
00:01:16,279 --> 00:01:19,335
从 Claude 4 开始，长的思考会被摘要
From Claude 4, long thinking was summarized,

24
00:01:19,335 --> 00:01:22,530
今天的 Claude API 只返回摘要
and today's Claude API returns only a summary.

25
00:01:22,766 --> 00:01:25,582
今天，思考是一个你自己选、自己付钱的设置
Today, thinking is a setting you choose and pay for.

26
00:01:25,902 --> 00:01:28,813
OpenAI 把它叫作 reasoning effort，也就是思考强度
OpenAI calls it reasoning effort.

27
00:01:28,863 --> 00:01:31,407
我们的菜单把它放在选模型的旁边
Our menu puts it next to the model choice,

28
00:01:31,407 --> 00:01:35,524
有 Luna、Terra 和另外两个模型，思考强度分三档：低、中、高
Luna, Terra and two others, with three levels: low, medium and high.

29
00:01:36,867 --> 00:01:39,064
看看一次调用里面发生了什么
Here is what happens inside one call.

30
00:01:39,384 --> 00:01:43,032
模型一次写一小段文字，叫作 token
A model writes one small piece of text at a time, a token.

31
00:01:43,352 --> 00:01:46,190
推理模型会先写一些给自己看的 token
A reasoning model first writes tokens for itself.

32
00:01:46,510 --> 00:01:48,110
那就是它的思考
Those are its thoughts.

33
00:01:50,017 --> 00:01:52,790
OpenAI 从不把这些 token 发回来
OpenAI never sends those tokens back.

34
00:01:53,110 --> 00:01:57,676
它们是隐藏的，但会占用上下文空间，而且按输出的价格计费
They stay hidden, but they take up room, and you pay for them at the output price.

35
00:01:57,917 --> 00:02:01,202
然后它才写回答，也就是我们那张 13 格的表
Only then does it write the answer, our thirteen-box form.

36
00:02:01,522 --> 00:02:03,741
所以我们的计时器能把两段分开
So our stopwatch can tell the two apart.

37
00:02:04,061 --> 00:02:08,442
思考，是到回答的第一个字到达为止的时间
Thinking is the time until the first character of the answer arrives:

38
00:02:08,442 --> 00:02:12,189
模型先读完请求，再用隐藏的 token 推理
the model reads the request, then reasons in hidden tokens.

39
00:02:12,509 --> 00:02:16,626
写，是从那里到模型写完；然后检查器开始运行
Writing runs from there until the model finishes; then the checker runs.

40
00:02:16,867 --> 00:02:19,790
思考强度决定模型最多可以想多少
The effort setting sets how much thinking the model may do.

41
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:24,580
即使设置一样，模型也会自己决定需要想多少
Even on the same setting, the model decides how much it needs:

42
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:27,320
你的问候想了 1.6 秒
your greeting thought for 1.6 seconds,

43
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,926
一个关于学校医疗中心的真实问题想了 13.5 秒
a real question about the student clinic for 13.5.

44
00:02:33,167 --> 00:02:37,540
既然思考是隐藏的，你到底在为什么付钱，又怎么知道？
If the thoughts are hidden, what exactly are you paying for, and how would you know?

45
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:44,261
每次回复最后都有一份 usage 报告
Every response ends with a usage report,

46
00:02:44,261 --> 00:02:48,152
它把推理 token 算在输出 token 里
and it counts the reasoning tokens inside the output tokens.

47
00:02:48,472 --> 00:02:49,972
我们的服务器读取这份报告
Our server reads it,

48
00:02:49,972 --> 00:02:53,720
价格表把这些数字换算成收据上的金额
and the price list turns those counts into the dollar figure on the receipt.

49
00:02:55,067 --> 00:02:56,838
等的时候，为什么要显示点什么？
Why show anything while you wait?

50
00:02:57,158 --> 00:02:59,220
决策记录说得很直白
The decision record puts it plainly:

51
00:02:59,220 --> 00:03:03,344
干等 10 到 30 秒，人不知道在发生什么
ten to thirty seconds of waiting, and nobody can tell what is happening.

52
00:03:03,664 --> 00:03:05,993
大多数聊天 app 的办法是流式输出
Most chat apps answer that by streaming:

53
00:03:05,993 --> 00:03:09,825
每写出几个词，就立刻送到你的屏幕上
every few words travel to your screen the moment they are written,

54
00:03:09,825 --> 00:03:12,048
走的是一条叫 server-sent events 的通道
over a pipe called server-sent events.

55
00:03:12,284 --> 00:03:15,484
我们的服务器确实从 OpenAI 收到了这条流
Our server does receive that stream from OpenAI.

56
00:03:15,804 --> 00:03:17,596
但它不把这些文字转发出去
But it does not pass the words on.

57
00:03:17,916 --> 00:03:20,008
它一边读这张逐渐填满的表
It reads the form as it fills,

58
00:03:20,008 --> 00:03:23,844
一边记下模型写到了哪一格、写了多少字
notes which box the model is in, counts the characters,

59
00:03:23,844 --> 00:03:28,518
然后只把进度发给页面，每次一小行 JSON
and sends the page only progress, one small line of JSON at a time.

60
00:03:28,767 --> 00:03:31,775
你看到的就是这些：正在思考，11 秒
That is what you watch: thinking, eleven seconds.

61
00:03:32,095 --> 00:03:35,956
正在写去处和步骤，已写 320 字
Writing the places to go, 320 characters so far.

62
00:03:36,276 --> 00:03:40,479
正在检查。在检查器看过之前，页面一个字也看不到
Checking. The page never sees a word before the checker has.

63
00:03:41,817 --> 00:03:46,702
为什么不像 Claude 那样直接流式显示文字，检查不过再收回？
Why not stream the words, the way Claude does, and pull them back if the checker objects?

64
00:03:50,450 --> 00:03:52,583
因为屏幕上说出去的话收不回来
Because a screen cannot unsay something.

65
00:03:52,903 --> 00:03:56,527
如果一个剂量或者一个编造的电话号码在屏幕上闪了两秒
If a dose or a made-up phone number flashes for two seconds,

66
00:03:56,527 --> 00:03:59,367
着急的家长可能已经截了图
a worried parent may already have a screenshot.

67
00:03:59,687 --> 00:04:03,357
所以决策记录写的是：流式传输进度，而不是文字
So the decision record says: stream the progress, not the text.

68
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,200
你要的是流式输出
You asked for streaming.

69
00:04:05,264 --> 00:04:08,897
agent 在无人值守时自己选了这种做法
The agent, working unattended, chose this kind on its own,

70
00:04:08,897 --> 00:04:13,094
并把它写成一份提议，还在等你点头
and wrote it down as a proposal that is still waiting for your yes.

71
00:04:14,433 --> 00:04:16,566
进度流式输出还有一招
Progress streaming has one more trick.

72
00:04:16,886 --> 00:04:21,900
表的前五格都和紧急程度有关，所以模型最先写它们
The form's first five boxes are all about urgency, so the model writes them first.

73
00:04:22,150 --> 00:04:26,941
前几格一说是紧急情况，服务器就打上紧急标记
The moment those first boxes say emergency, the server raises a flag,

74
00:04:26,941 --> 00:04:30,273
页面显示一段我们自己写好的提醒
and the page shows a warning we wrote ourselves:

75
00:04:30,273 --> 00:04:33,883
可能危及生命，不用等，现在就打 911
possibly life-threatening, don't wait, call 911 now.

76
00:04:34,116 --> 00:04:37,865
在一次真实测试里，提醒在第 3.5 秒出现
In a real test, the warning appeared at 3.5 seconds,

77
00:04:37,865 --> 00:04:40,964
检查过的回答在大约第 21 秒才到
and the checked answer at about 21 seconds.

78
00:04:41,284 --> 00:04:45,764
而且紧急判断从不收回，所以那个回答一定和提醒一致
And since an emergency is never taken back, that answer is bound to agree.

79
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:52,977
检查过的回答终于到达时，页面最多用两秒半把它展示出来
When the checked answer finally arrives, the page plays it out in at most two and a half seconds:

80
00:04:52,977 --> 00:04:55,825
句子逐字打出来，列表整块出现
sentences type themselves, lists drop in whole.

81
00:04:56,145 --> 00:04:57,738
看起来像流式输出
It looks like streaming.

82
00:04:57,788 --> 00:05:00,412
其实是一段回放，回放的是已经通过检查的文字
It is a replay of text that has already passed.

83
00:05:00,650 --> 00:05:03,637
紧急回答跳过这段表演，立刻全部显示
Emergency answers skip the show and appear at once.

84
00:05:03,957 --> 00:05:05,939
停止按钮也是真的停止
And the stop button really stops:

85
00:05:05,939 --> 00:05:10,442
页面挂断，服务器取消它正在付钱的那次模型调用
the page hangs up, and the server cancels the model call it was paying for.

86
00:05:11,783 --> 00:05:16,284
周三上午，波士顿时间，流式输出在 20 分钟之内做好了
On Wednesday morning, Boston time, the streaming went in within twenty minutes.

87
00:05:16,604 --> 00:05:19,275
几分钟后，菜单加了一条说明
A few minutes later, a note for the menu:

88
00:05:19,275 --> 00:05:22,337
切换模型或思考强度会从一份新的缓存开始
switching model or effort starts a fresh cache,

89
00:05:22,337 --> 00:05:26,311
所以在 Terra 上，那第一次回答大约贵 5 倍
so on Terra that first answer costs about five times as much.

90
00:05:26,550 --> 00:05:30,042
那天剩下的很多时间，花在了 review 发现的问题上
Much of the rest of the day went to what reviews found:

91
00:05:30,042 --> 00:05:34,359
在停止、重试和断线时都保住 911 提醒
keeping the 911 warning through stop, retry and dropped connections,

92
00:05:34,359 --> 00:05:39,183
还有一个测试，只要模型原文里任意连续
and a test that fails if any four consecutive characters of the model's text

93
00:05:39,183 --> 00:05:42,230
4 个字符在结果之前出现在进度行里，它就失败
show up in the progress lines before the result.

94
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:47,478
这个测试证明：检查器放行之前，没有一个字会到达页面
That test is the proof that no words reach the page before the checker has passed them.

95
00:05:48,817 --> 00:05:51,740
那么，「思考了 22 秒」后面是什么？
So what sits behind "thought for 22 seconds"?

96
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:55,277
Claude 的 app 在思考时也显示计时器
Claude's app also shows a timer while it thinks,

97
00:05:55,277 --> 00:05:59,633
并且和 ChatGPT 一样，点开是一段模型推理的摘要
and, like ChatGPT, opens onto a summary of the model's reasoning.

98
00:05:59,953 --> 00:06:01,600
我们的点开是一张收据
Ours opens onto a receipt:

99
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:06,353
用时、依据、检查、判断、模型和价格
the timings, the sources, the check, the judgment, the model and the price.

100
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,776
原因写在决策记录里
The reason is in the decision record.

101
00:06:09,096 --> 00:06:13,363
推理原文里可能有诊断性的猜测，而且没有任何东西检查过它
Raw reasoning may contain diagnostic guesses, and nothing has checked it.

102
00:06:13,683 --> 00:06:17,694
在医疗产品里，屏幕上的一个猜测，读起来就像一个诊断
In a medical product, a guess on screen reads like a diagnosis.

103
00:06:19,033 --> 00:06:20,476
还能往哪里走？
Where could this go?

104
00:06:20,526 --> 00:06:23,790
OpenAI 可以返回隐藏推理的摘要
OpenAI can return a summary of the hidden reasoning.

105
00:06:24,110 --> 00:06:27,735
但摘要也是模型写的，所以在任何人看到之前
But a summary is written by a model too, so it would have to pass the same checker before anyone sees it.

106
00:06:27,735 --> 00:06:29,806
它也得通过同一个检查器
But a summary is written by a model too, so it would have to pass the same checker before anyone sees it.

107
00:06:30,126 --> 00:06:34,265
进度行可以说出真实的步骤，比如正在核对诊所的营业时间
The progress line could name real steps, like checking the clinic's hours.

108
00:06:34,585 --> 00:06:37,159
agent 还提过一个只给开发者用的开关
And the agent raised a developer-only switch

109
00:06:37,159 --> 00:06:39,790
在调提示词时看没检查过的草稿
to see unchecked drafts while tuning prompts.

110
00:06:40,110 --> 00:06:41,483
它没有被做出来
It was not built.

111
00:06:41,533 --> 00:06:43,154
有三个决定在等你
Three decisions wait for you.

112
00:06:43,474 --> 00:06:48,052
只流进度的流式输出和模型菜单，被写成了提议
Progress-only streaming and the model menu are written down as proposals;

113
00:06:48,052 --> 00:06:50,685
开发者开关，被写成了一个待定的问题
the developer switch, as an open question.

114
00:06:52,033 --> 00:06:54,102
所以，思考了 22 秒
So, thought for 22 seconds.

115
00:06:54,422 --> 00:06:59,414
先是思考：模型写给自己的隐藏 token，要付钱，但从不发回
First thinking: hidden tokens the model writes for itself, billed but never sent.

116
00:06:59,734 --> 00:07:05,324
然后是写，我们的服务器一格一格地盯着，只转发进度，不转发文字
Then writing, which our server watches box by box, passing on progress but not words.

117
00:07:05,644 --> 00:07:08,950
前几格一说紧急，就提前给出提醒
An early warning when the first boxes say emergency.

118
00:07:09,270 --> 00:07:11,425
检查器通过之后，再回放一遍
A replay once the checker has passed it.

119
00:07:11,745 --> 00:07:13,708
最后，用一张收据代替思考内容
And a receipt instead of the thoughts.

120
00:07:13,950 --> 00:07:15,329
三个问题
Three questions.

121
00:07:15,379 --> 00:07:17,854
我们的计时器到底把什么叫作思考？
What exactly does our stopwatch call thinking?

122
00:07:18,174 --> 00:07:21,118
为什么和紧急程度有关的几格排在表的最前面？
Why do the urgency boxes come first in the form?

123
00:07:21,438 --> 00:07:24,616
一段推理摘要要先经过什么，才能给人看？
And what would a reasoning summary need before it could be shown?

124
00:07:24,866 --> 00:07:26,494
下一集讲页面本身
Next time, the page itself:

125
00:07:26,494 --> 00:07:31,074
我们从 Claude 的 app 学了什么、拒绝了什么，还能发明什么
what we copied from Claude's app, what we refused, and what we could invent.
